// REJECTS: Unexpected token '~owner:'
//
// The companion to ordering-constraint-clauses.pure, which moves ~message to the front.
// This one swaps only the two OPTIONAL leading clauses -- ~externalId before ~owner -- and
// is still a parse error, because the sequence is positional throughout, not just around
// the required ~function.
//
// This is the shape most likely to slip through a rewrite. Moving ~message ahead of
// ~function looks wrong to a human reader; swapping two adjacent metadata annotations that
// carry no dependency on one another looks like formatting. A parser that loops over
// "which clause is next" accepts it, and the model then loads on one engine only.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::SwappedConstraintHead
[
   swapped
   (
      ~externalId: 'RISK-003'
      ~owner: riskOps
      ~function: $this.code->length() > 2
   )
]
{
   code: String[1];
}
